At H${=}96$, Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+} achieves $\mathbf{27/27}$ match-or-beat across all five cross-backbones and all six datasets, with margins of $-8.5\%$ to $-31.7\%$. The recipe generalizes across all normalization regimes: RevIN (MOMENT-large), LayerNorm (Moirai, Moirai-MoE), no instance norm (Chronos, Timer-XL).

\textbf{The stronger picture emerges at longer horizons.} We extend to the full $5$ backbones $\times$ $6$ datasets $\times$ $4$ horizons grid (Table~\ref{tab:residual_ia_plus_mhcb}).

